// Copyright (c) 2026 Roshan. All rights reserved.// Proprietary license — see LICENSE file for details.package com.roshan.persona.productivity.alarm/** * NOUS — Encrypted Payload (Module 14 v1.2). * * Shared AES-GCM encrypted payload used by both the note module * ([com.roshan.persona.productivity.note.NoteEncryptionHelper]) and the * reminder module ([com.roshan.persona.productivity.reminder.ReminderEncryptionHelper]). * * Lives in the `alarm` package because it is the lowest-level utility * package in the productivity module (alarms don't depend on reminders or * notes, but both notes and reminders need this type). Keeping it here * avoids a circular dependency between `note` and `reminder`. * * ## Real Android APIs Used (transitively via encryption helpers) * * | Operation | API | * |-----------|-----| * | IV generation | `Cipher.getInstance("AES/GCM/NoPadding").init(ENCRYPT_MODE, key)` (AndroidKeystore-generated fresh IV per call) | * | Ciphertext | `Cipher.doFinal(plaintext.toByteArray(UTF_8))` (ciphertext + GCM auth tag) | * | Encoding | `android.util.Base64.encodeToString(..., Base64.NO_WRAP)` | * * ## Security Properties * * - **AES-256-GCM**: authenticated encryption (confidentiality + integrity). * - **Per-call IV**: a fresh 12-byte IV is generated for every encrypt call *   (AndroidKeystore enforces this via `setRandomizedEncryptionRequired(true)`). * - **Key never leaves Keystore**: the SecretKey is opaque; raw bytes are *   never accessible to the app process. * * @property ivBase64         initialization vector (12 bytes for GCM, Base64-encoded). * @property ciphertextBase64 ciphertext + GCM auth tag (Base64-encoded). */data class EncryptedData(    val ivBase64: String,    val ciphertextBase64: String,)